<html>
<body>
<h2>JavaScript array method</h2>
<h2>join()and pop()</h2>
<P>the join() method joins array elements into a string and the pop() method removes the last elements from an array.</P>
<p id="myjoin"></p>
<p id="myfirstpop"></p>
<P id="mysecondpop"></P>
<script>
var fruits =["tomato", "potato", "brinjal", "capsicum"];
document.getElementById("myjoin").innerHTML= fruits.join("*");
document.getElementById("myfirstpop").innerHTML = fruits;fruits.pop;
document.getElementById("mysecondpop").innerHTML = fruits;
</script>
</body>
</html>